Q: Flutter : add a space between title and subtitle in ListTile A: <pre><code>// এটি একটি ডামি লিস্ট কার্ডের কোড
Widget matchCard(String title, String time, String entryFee, String prize) {
  return Card(
    child: ListTile(
      title: Text(title, style: TextStyle(fontWeight: FontWeight.bold)),
      subtitle: Text(&quot;Time: $time&quot;),
      trailing: Column(
        children: [
          Text(&quot;Prize: $prize&quot;),
          ElevatedButton(onPressed: () {}, child: Text(&quot;Join Fee: $entryFee&quot;)),
        ],
      ),
    ),
  );
}
</code></pre>

Q: Pass Storage value to object Ionic 2 A: <p><code>storage.get()</code> is async.<br />
So <code>this.userData</code> is created <strong>before</strong> <code>this.name</code> gets its value from storage.</p>
<p>At this moment:</p>
<pre><code>nama: this.name
</code></pre>
<p><code>this.name</code> is still <code>undefined</code>.</p>
<p>Move the object creation inside the <code>.then()</code> callback:</p>
<pre><code>name: any;
userData: {
  id: string,
  nama: string,
  no_hp: string,
  email: string
};

constructor(
  public navCtrl: NavController,
  public storage: Storage
) {

  this.storage.get('name').then((nama) =&gt; {

    this.name = nama;

    this.userData = {
      id: '0404040404',
      nama: this.name,
      no_hp: '082211590346',
      email: 'rifqyzackya@gmail.com'
    };

    console.log(this.userData);

  });

}
</code></pre>
<p>You can even simplify it:</p>
<pre><code>this.storage.get('name').then((nama) =&gt; {

  this.userData = {
    id: '0404040404',
    nama: nama,
    no_hp: '082211590346',
    email: 'rifqyzackya@gmail.com'
  };

});
</code></pre>

Q: How to inject credentials for SOCKS5 proxy in Playwright launch? A: <p>you should use proxy url format <code>socks5://username:password@IP:PORT</code></p>
<p>for example:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const { chromium } = require('playwright');

(async () =&gt; {
  const proxyHost = '31.59.20.176';
  const proxyPort = 6754;
  const proxyUser = 'myuser';
  const proxyPass = 'mypassword';

  const proxyUrl = `socks5://${proxyUser}:${proxyPass}@${proxyHost}:${proxyPort}`;

  const browser = await chromium.launch({
    headless: false,

    proxy: {
      server: `socks5://${proxyHost}:${proxyPort}`,
      username: proxyUser,
      password: proxyPass,
    },

    args: [
      `--proxy-server=${proxyUrl}`,
    ],
  });

  const page = await browser.newPage();

  await page.goto('https://httpbin.org/ip');

  console.log(await page.textContent('body'));

  await browser.close();
})();
</code></pre>
<p>or full using context</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const { chromium } = require('playwright');

(async () =&gt; {
  const proxyHost = '31.59.20.176';
  const proxyPort = 6754;
  const proxyUser = 'myuser';
  const proxyPass = 'mypassword';

  const proxyUrl = `socks5://${proxyUser}:${proxyPass}@${proxyHost}:${proxyPort}`;

  const browser = await chromium.launch({
    headless: false,

    proxy: {
      server: `socks5://${proxyHost}:${proxyPort}`,
      username: proxyUser,
      password: proxyPass,
    },

    args: [
      `--proxy-server=${proxyUrl}`,
    ],
  });

  const context = await browser.newContext({
    proxy: {
      server: `socks5://${proxyHost}:${proxyPort}`,
      username: proxyUser,
      password: proxyPass,
    },
  });

  const page = await context.newPage();

  await page.goto('https://httpbin.org/ip');

  console.log(await page.textContent('body'));

  await browser.close();
})();
</code></pre>
